{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>שלא</b> — And this grass has no use, and this is the opposite of 'he shall come, he shall come with rejoicing, bearing his sheaves' (Psalms 126:6)." "<b>וחצנו</b> — like 'גם חצני נערתי' (Genesis 41:12) ['and my boyhood arms'], and it is a verb." "<b>מעמר</b> — gatherer of the sheaves."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 129, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:29.586026648Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}